  "notes": [
    "Timeout/cancellation/maximum-attempt/partial roll-up of the graph and retryable/ambiguous Provider failures are deterministic fixture Evidence (allowed by T24 'controlled fake failure/non-effect cases'); F4 re-runs them at the exact product tree. Real graph retry is exercised only if D4 records a real failed attempt, under its own retry authority (runner --retry-child).",
    "Installer interruption/partial upgrade resume is covered by the native T22 suite per row; envelope A covers owned upgrade and downgrade refusal with published RCs.",
    "Drift expectation follows cmd/lingo/s9_dogfood_blackbox_test.go: a lost established marker returns status failure (exit 1) with no Provider effect."
  ]
